abstract: >
  A three-part living document: a literature review challenging the "weakest link"
  framing and fact-based awareness training in cybersecurity (Part I); an
  applied practitioner framework, the Human Firewall Framework (HFF), built on
  Cognitive Security, dual-process theory, persuasion science, memory
  neuroscience, inoculation theory, and behavior change science (Part II); and
  a worked case study mapping the framework onto ten social engineering
  attack vectors (Part III).
